-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 2, regulations 106 to 111: when a reduction takes effect,
-- how it is suspended and ended, and how much it takes off an award.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. When the Secretary of State "determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced" is a stated date or assessment
-- period, not a judgment the rules make. Amounts of money are in pounds; days are whole days.

§ `Chapter 2 — When a reduction takes effect, and how much it is`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 106 — Start of the reduction`

-- A reduction period takes effect from (a) the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the award
-- is to be reduced (but see also regulation 107(2)); (b) if the award for that period is not reduced in that period, the first day of the
-- next assessment period; or (c) if the award for the period in (a) or (b) is already subject to a reduction because of a previous
-- failure, the first day in respect of which the award is no longer subject to that reduction. Where (c) applies it governs, then (b),
-- then (a) (fork F-106-1). If (c) applies and the day is not yet known, the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:1699 | When reduction to have effect
-- src:1700 | 106 Start of the reduction
-- src:1701 | A reduction period determined in relation to a sanctionable failure takes effect from—
-- src:1702 | (a) the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act (but see also regulation 107(2));
-- src:1703 | (b) if the amount of the award of universal credit for the assessment period referred to in paragraph (a) is not reduced in that period, the first day of the next assessment period; or
-- src:1704 | (c) if the amount of the award for the assessment period referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) is already subject to a reduction because of a previous sanctionable failure, the first day in respect of which the amount of the award is no longer subject to that reduction.
@ref reg 106 (src:1699-1704)
GIVEN `first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the award for that assessment period is not reduced in that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day of the next assessment period` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the award for the assessment period in paragraph (a) or (b) is already subject to a reduction because of a previous sanctionable failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day in respect of which the amount of the award is no longer subject to that reduction` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 106 — the day from which the reduction period takes effect` `first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced` `the amount of the award for that assessment period is not reduced in that period` `first day of the next assessment period` `the amount of the award for the assessment period in paragraph (a) or (b) is already subject to a reduction because of a previous sanctionable failure` `first day in respect of which the amount of the award is no longer subject to that reduction` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the award for the assessment period in paragraph (a) or (b) is already subject to a reduction because of a previous sanctionable failure`
    THEN `first day in respect of which the amount of the award is no longer subject to that reduction`
    ELSE IF `the amount of the award for that assessment period is not reduced in that period`
         THEN JUST `first day of the next assessment period`
         ELSE JUST `first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 107 — Reduction period to continue where award terminates`

-- Paragraph (1): if an award terminates while there is an outstanding reduction period, the period continues to run as if a daily reduction
-- were being applied; and if the claimant becomes entitled to a new award (as single or joint claimant) before that period expires, the new
-- award is subject to a reduction for the remainder of the total outstanding reduction period. The period runs from the day after the award
-- terminates (fork F-107-1), so on the day the new award begins it has run for that day minus the day of termination, less one, days.
-- src:1705 | 107 Reduction period to continue where award terminates
-- src:1706 | (1) If an award of universal credit terminates while there is an outstanding reduction period, the period continues to run as if a daily reduction were being applied and if the claimant becomes entitled to a new award (whether as single or joint claimant) before that period expires, that award is subject to a reduction for the remainder of the total outstanding reduction period.
@ref reg 107(1) (src:1705-1706)
GIVEN `total outstanding reduction period when the award terminated` IS A NUMBER
      `date on which the award terminated` IS A DATE
      `date on which the claimant becomes entitled to a new award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 107(1) — the remainder of the total outstanding reduction period when the new award begins` `total outstanding reduction period when the award terminated` `date on which the award terminated` `date on which the claimant becomes entitled to a new award` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, `total outstanding reduction period when the award terminated` MINUS ((Day `date on which the claimant becomes entitled to a new award` MINUS Day `date on which the award terminated`) MINUS 1))

@ref reg 107(1) (src:1706)
GIVEN remainder IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 107(1) — the new award is subject to a reduction` remainder MEANS
    remainder GREATER THAN 0

-- Paragraph (2): if an award terminates before the Secretary of State determines that the award is to be reduced for a failure, and that
-- determination is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award, the reduction period has effect for the purposes of paragraph (1)
-- as if the determination had been made on the day before the previous award terminated.
-- src:1707 | (2) If an award of universal credit terminates before the Secretary of State determines that the amount of the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act in relation to a sanctionable failure and that determination is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award the reduction period in relation to that failure is to have effect for the purposes of paragraph (1) as if that determination had been made on the day before the previous award terminated.
@ref reg 107(2) (src:1707)
GIVEN `the previous award terminated before the Secretary of State determined that the amount of the award is to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the previous award terminated` IS A DATE
      `date on which the Secretary of State makes the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 107(2) — the day on which the determination is treated as made` `the previous award terminated before the Secretary of State determined that the amount of the award is to be reduced` `the determination is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award` `date on which the previous award terminated` `date on which the Secretary of State makes the determination` MEANS
    IF `the previous award terminated before the Secretary of State determined that the amount of the award is to be reduced` AND `the determination is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award`
    THEN `date on which the previous award terminated` MINUS 1
    ELSE `date on which the Secretary of State makes the determination`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 108 — Suspension of a reduction where fraud penalty applies`

-- Paragraph (1): a reduction is suspended for any period during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 applies to
-- the award. Paragraph (2): the reduction ceases to have effect on the day on which that period begins and begins again on the day after
-- that period ends. A period with no end yet has no day on which the reduction begins again.
-- out of range: sections 6B, 7 and 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (not among the inputs): the dates they fix are stated inputs
-- src:1708 | 108 Suspension of a reduction where fraud penalty applies
-- src:1709 | (1) A reduction in the amount of an award under section 26 or 27 of the Act is to be suspended for any period during which the provisions of section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 apply to the award.
-- src:1710 | (2) The reduction ceases to have effect on the day on which that period begins and begins again on the day after that period ends.
@ref reg 108 (src:1708-1710)
GIVEN `first day of the period during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 applies to the award` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `last day of that period` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 108 — the reduction is suspended on the day` `first day of the period during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 applies to the award` `last day of that period` `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `first day of the period during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 applies to the award`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST starts THEN
        ((Day `the day asked about` MINUS Day starts) AT LEAST 0)
        AND `the period has not ended by the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the period has not ended by the day asked about` MEANS
            CONSIDER `last day of that period`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST ends THEN (Day `the day asked about` MINUS Day ends) AT MOST 0

