§§ `Regulation 109 — When a reduction is to be terminated`

-- Paragraph (1)(b): the claimant's monthly earnings during the period or periods of paid work were equal to or exceeded (i) the claimant's
-- individual threshold, (ia) where the claimant has no individual threshold, the amount paid at the hourly rate in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to
-- (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours a week, converted to a month by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12 (rounded to
-- the penny by regulation 6(1); regulation 6(1A) does not name regulation 109: fork F-41-1), or (ii) if regulation 90(4) applies (the apprentice's threshold) the amount applicable under that
-- paragraph. Each route applies in its own case, and the monthly earnings of every month must reach the amount (fork F-109-1).
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- src:1711 | 109 When a reduction is to be terminated
-- src:1712 | (1) A reduction in the amount of an award under section 26 or 27 of the Act is to be terminated where—
-- src:1713 | (a) since the date of the most recent sanctionable failure which gave rise to a reduction, the claimant has been in paid work for a period of, or for periods amounting in total to, at least six months; and
-- src:1714 | (b) the claimant's monthly earnings during that period or those periods were equal to or exceeded—
-- src:1715 | (i) the claimant's individual threshold, ...
-- src:1716 | (ia) where the claimant has no individual threshold, the amount that a person would be paid at the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12, or
-- src:1717 | (ii) if paragraph (4) of regulation 90 applies (threshold for an apprentice) the amount applicable under that paragraph.
@ref reg 109(1) (src:1711-1717)
GIVEN earnings IS A NUMBER
      `individual threshold` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 109(1)(b) — a month's earnings equal or exceed the amount` earnings `individual threshold` `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `the expected number of hours per week` `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    `the individual threshold route, or the 16 hours route when there is none`
    OR `reg 90(4) — the apprentice's monthly earnings equal or exceed the threshold` `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` earnings `the expected number of hours per week` `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
    WHERE
        `the individual threshold route, or the 16 hours route when there is none` MEANS
            CONSIDER `individual threshold`
            WHEN JUST threshold THEN earnings AT LEAST threshold
            WHEN NOTHING THEN earnings AT LEAST (`core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate` 16 `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`))

-- Paragraph (1): a reduction is to be terminated where (a) since the date of the most recent sanctionable failure which gave rise to a
-- reduction, the claimant has been in paid work for a period of, or periods amounting in total to, at least six months, and (b) the
-- claimant's monthly earnings during that period or those periods reached the amount. The months of paid work are a number the caller gives;
-- the text does not say how part-months add up (fork F-109-2). No months of earnings given counts for nothing, so the test fails.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
@ref reg 109(1) (src:1712-1717)
GIVEN `months of paid work since the date of the most recent sanctionable failure which gave rise to a reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `monthly earnings in each month of that period or those periods` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `individual threshold` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expected number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 109(1) — the reduction is to be terminated` `months of paid work since the date of the most recent sanctionable failure which gave rise to a reduction` `monthly earnings in each month of that period or those periods` `individual threshold` `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `the expected number of hours per week` `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    (`months of paid work since the date of the most recent sanctionable failure which gave rise to a reduction` AT LEAST 6)
    AND (NOT (null `monthly earnings in each month of that period or those periods`))
    AND (all (GIVEN e YIELD `reg 109(1)(b) — a month's earnings equal or exceed the amount` e `individual threshold` `hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `the claimant is employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `the expected number of hours per week` `the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`) `monthly earnings in each month of that period or those periods`)

-- Paragraph (2): the termination has effect (a) where the date on which paragraph (1) is satisfied falls within a period of entitlement to
-- universal credit, from the beginning of the assessment period in which that date falls; or (b) where that date falls outside a period of
-- entitlement, from the beginning of the first assessment period in relation to any subsequent award. NOTHING when the day needed is not given.
-- src:1718 | (2) The termination of the reduction has effect—
-- src:1719 | (a) where the date on which paragraph (1) is satisfied falls within a period of entitlement to universal credit, from the beginning of the assessment period in which that date falls; or
-- src:1720 | (b) where that date falls outside a period of entitlement to universal credit, from the beginning of the first assessment period in relation to any subsequent award.
@ref reg 109(2) (src:1718-1720)
GIVEN `the date on which paragraph (1) is satisfied falls within a period of entitlement to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day of the assessment period in which that date falls` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `first day of the first assessment period in relation to any subsequent award` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 109(2) — the day from which the termination of the reduction has effect` `the date on which paragraph (1) is satisfied falls within a period of entitlement to universal credit` `first day of the assessment period in which that date falls` `first day of the first assessment period in relation to any subsequent award` MEANS
    IF `the date on which paragraph (1) is satisfied falls within a period of entitlement to universal credit`
    THEN `first day of the assessment period in which that date falls`
    ELSE `first day of the first assessment period in relation to any subsequent award`

-- Paragraph (3): a claimant treated as having earned income under regulation 62 (the minimum income floor) for an assessment period is taken
-- to have monthly earnings equal to their individual threshold for it. NOTHING when the claimant has no individual threshold.
-- out of range: regulation 62 (piece uc2): whether the claimant is treated as having earned income is a stated input
-- src:1721 | (3) A claimant who is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 (minimum income floor) in respect of an assessment period is to be taken to have monthly earnings equal to their individual threshold in respect of ... that assessment period.
@ref reg 109(3) (src:1721)
GIVEN `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 in respect of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `individual threshold` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 109(3) — the monthly earnings the claimant is taken to have` `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 in respect of the assessment period` `the claimant's monthly earnings` `individual threshold` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 in respect of the assessment period`
    THEN `individual threshold`
    ELSE JUST `the claimant's monthly earnings`

