§§ `Regulation 111 — Daily reduction rate`

-- Facts at the end of the assessment period that paragraphs (2) and (3) turn on. "By virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)" is a fact
-- the caller reads off regulation 89 (the rules in uc4-part8-ch1-groups.l4).
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
-- src:1738 | 111 Daily reduction rate
-- src:1739 | (1) The daily reduction rate for the purposes of regulation 110 is, unless paragraph (2), or (3) applies, an amount equal to the amount of the standard allowance that is applicable to the award multiplied by 12 and divided by 365.
-- src:1740 | (2) The daily reduction rate is 40% of the rate set out in paragraph (1) if, at the end of the assessment period—
-- src:1741 | (a) the claimant is aged 16 or 17;
-- src:1742 | (b) the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimant subject to no work-related requirements) by virtue of—
-- src:1743 | (i) subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1), or
-- src:1744 | (ii) regulation 89(1)(c),(d) or (f) (adopter, claimant within 11 weeks before or 15 weeks after confinement or responsible foster parent of a child under the age of 1); or
-- src:1745 | (c) the claimant falls within section 20 (claimant subject to work-focused interview only).
-- src:1746 | (3) The daily reduction rate is nil if, at the end of the assessment period, the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity.
-- src:1747 | (4) The amount of the rate in paragraphs (1) and (2) is to be rounded down to the nearest 10 pence.
-- src:1748 | (5) In the case of joint claimants-
-- src:1749 | (a) each joint claimant is considered individually for the purpose of determining the rate applicable under paragraphs (1) to (3); and
-- src:1750 | (b) half of any applicable rate is applied to each joint claimant accordingly.
@ref reg 111(2) and (3) (src:1740-1746)
DECLARE `Position at the end of the assessment period` HAS
    `the claimant is aged 16 or 17`                                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph (2): 40% of the rate in paragraph (1) if, at the end of the assessment period, (a) the claimant is aged 16 or 17, (b) falls within
-- section 19 by virtue of section 19(2)(c) or regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f), or (c) falls within section 20.
@ref reg 111(2) (src:1740-1745)
GIVEN position IS A `Position at the end of the assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 111(2) — the daily reduction rate is 40% of the rate in paragraph (1)` position MEANS
    (position's `the claimant is aged 16 or 17`)
    OR (position's `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)`)
    OR (position's `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)`)
    OR (position's `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act`)

-- Paragraph (3): the rate is nil if, at the end of the assessment period, the claimant falls within section 19 by virtue of having limited
-- capability for work and work-related activity.
@ref reg 111(3) (src:1746)
GIVEN position IS A `Position at the end of the assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 111(3) — the daily reduction rate is nil` position MEANS
    position's `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- Paragraph (1): the standard allowance applicable to the award multiplied by 12 and divided by 365. Paragraph (4): the rate in paragraphs
-- (1) and (2) is rounded down to the nearest 10 pence. The 40% of paragraph (2) is taken of the unrounded amount of paragraph (1), and the
-- result rounded once (fork F-111-1). Where both paragraph (2) and paragraph (3) apply, paragraph (3) governs (fork F-111-2).
@ref reg 111(1) (src:1739)
@ref reg 111(4) (src:1747)
GIVEN position IS A `Position at the end of the assessment period`
      `standard allowance applicable to the award` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 111(1) to (4) — the daily reduction rate for one claimant before paragraph (5)` position `standard allowance applicable to the award` MEANS
    IF `reg 111(3) — the daily reduction rate is nil` position
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `reg 111(2) — the daily reduction rate is 40% of the rate in paragraph (1)` position
         THEN `rounded down to the nearest 10 pence` (0.4 TIMES `the amount in paragraph (1)`)
         ELSE `rounded down to the nearest 10 pence` `the amount in paragraph (1)`
    WHERE
        `the amount in paragraph (1)` MEANS (`standard allowance applicable to the award` TIMES 12) DIVIDED BY 365
        `rounded down to the nearest 10 pence` x MEANS (FLOOR (x TIMES 10)) DIVIDED BY 10

-- Paragraph (5): in the case of joint claimants each is considered individually for the rate under paragraphs (1) to (3), and half of any
-- applicable rate is applied to each joint claimant. The half is taken of the rate after paragraph (4) has rounded it (fork F-111-3).
-- src:1748 | (5) In the case of joint claimants-
-- src:1749 | (a) each joint claimant is considered individually for the purpose of determining the rate applicable under paragraphs (1) to (3); and
-- src:1750 | (b) half of any applicable rate is applied to each joint claimant accordingly.
@ref reg 111(5) (src:1748-1750)
GIVEN position IS A `Position at the end of the assessment period`
      `standard allowance applicable to the award` IS A NUMBER
      `the award is a joint claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 111 — the daily reduction rate applied to the claimant` position `standard allowance applicable to the award` `the award is a joint claim` MEANS
    IF `the award is a joint claim`
    THEN (`reg 111(1) to (4) — the daily reduction rate for one claimant before paragraph (5)` position `standard allowance applicable to the award`) DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE `reg 111(1) to (4) — the daily reduction rate for one claimant before paragraph (5)` position `standard allowance applicable to the award`

