§§ `Regulation 110 — Amount of reduction for each assessment period`

-- Step 1: take the number of days (a) in the assessment period, or (b) if lower, in the total outstanding reduction period, and deduct any days
-- in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended under regulation 108. A number of days is not taken below nought (fork F-110-1).
-- src:1722 | Amount of reduction
-- src:1723 | 110 Amount of reduction for each assessment period
-- src:1724 | Where it has been determined that an award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act, the amount of the reduction for each assessment period in respect of which a reduction has effect is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:1725 | Step 1
-- src:1726 | Take the number of days—
-- src:1727 | (a) in the assessment period; or
-- src:1728 | (b) if lower, in the total outstanding reduction period,
-- src:1729 | and deduct any days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108.
-- src:1730 | Step 2
-- src:1731 | Multiply the number of days produced by step 1 by the daily reduction rate (see regulation 111).
-- src:1732 | Step 3
-- src:1733 | If necessary, adjust the amount produced by step 2 so that it does not exceed—
-- src:1734 | (a) the amount of the standard allowance applicable to the award; or
-- src:1735 | (b) in the case of a joint claim where a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one claimant, half the amount of that standard allowance.
-- src:1736 | Step 4
-- src:1737 | Deduct the amount produced by steps 2 and 3 from the amount of the award for the assessment period after any deduction has been made in accordance with Part 7 (the benefit cap).
@ref reg 110 Step 1 (src:1724-1729)
GIVEN `number of days in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER
      `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period` IS A NUMBER
      `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 110 Step 1 — the number of days` `number of days in the assessment period` `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period` `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, (minimum (LIST `number of days in the assessment period`, `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period`)) MINUS `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108`)

-- Step 2: multiply the number of days produced by step 1 by the daily reduction rate (regulation 111).
@ref reg 110 Step 2 (src:1730-1731)
GIVEN `the number of days produced by step 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the daily reduction rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 110 Step 2 — the number of days multiplied by the daily reduction rate` `the number of days produced by step 1` `the daily reduction rate` MEANS
    `the number of days produced by step 1` TIMES `the daily reduction rate`

-- Step 3: adjust the amount produced by step 2 so that it does not exceed (a) the standard allowance applicable to the award, or (b) in the case
-- of a joint claim where a determination under section 26 or 27 applies only to one claimant, half that standard allowance.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 110 Step 3 (src:1732-1735)
GIVEN `the amount produced by step 2` IS A NUMBER
      `standard allowance applicable to the award` IS A NUMBER
      `the award is a joint claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 110 Step 3 — the amount adjusted so that it does not exceed the limit` `the amount produced by step 2` `standard allowance applicable to the award` `the award is a joint claim` `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants` MEANS
    minimum (LIST `the amount produced by step 2`, `the limit`)
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS
            IF `the award is a joint claim` AND `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants`
            THEN `standard allowance applicable to the award` DIVIDED BY 2
            ELSE `standard allowance applicable to the award`

-- The amount of the reduction for the assessment period: steps 1 to 3 together.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 110 (src:1723-1735)
GIVEN `number of days in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER
      `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period` IS A NUMBER
      `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108` IS A NUMBER
      `the daily reduction rate` IS A NUMBER
      `standard allowance applicable to the award` IS A NUMBER
      `the award is a joint claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 110 — the amount of the reduction for the assessment period` `number of days in the assessment period` `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period` `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108` `the daily reduction rate` `standard allowance applicable to the award` `the award is a joint claim` `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants` MEANS
    `reg 110 Step 3 — the amount adjusted so that it does not exceed the limit`
        (`reg 110 Step 2 — the number of days multiplied by the daily reduction rate`
            (`reg 110 Step 1 — the number of days` `number of days in the assessment period` `number of days in the total outstanding reduction period` `number of days in that assessment period for which the reduction is suspended in accordance with regulation 108`)
            `the daily reduction rate`)
        `standard allowance applicable to the award`
        `the award is a joint claim`
        `a determination under section 26 or 27 of the Act applies only in relation to one of the joint claimants`

-- Step 4: deduct the amount produced by steps 2 and 3 from the amount of the award for the assessment period after any deduction has been
-- made under Part 7 (the benefit cap). The text does not stop the answer falling below nothing when the reduction is more than the award, and
-- the rule does not either (fork F-110-2).
@ref reg 110 Step 4 (src:1736-1737)
GIVEN `the amount of the award for the assessment period after any deduction under Part 7` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount produced by steps 2 and 3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 110 Step 4 — the amount of the award after the reduction` `the amount of the award for the assessment period after any deduction under Part 7` `the amount produced by steps 2 and 3` MEANS
    `the amount of the award for the assessment period after any deduction under Part 7` MINUS `the amount produced by steps 2 and 3`
